    "narrative": "The projected output for LawDog today is anchored by **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Tyler Freeman** (71.80), who represent our highest-upside plays. **Lawrence Butler** benefits from an excellent matchup against Sandy Alcantara; while Alcantara is a capable arm, his 4.48 xERA provides the right environment for **Lawrence Butler** to capitalize on a +10% park factor and the sustained momentum of a top-three lineup placement. Similarly, **Tyler Freeman** thrives against the southpaw Robbie Ray. Despite the concern regarding Ray's ability to limit stolen bases, the +14% park boost and the +18% SP skill advantage propel **Tyler Freeman** into our primary utility-adjacent role, offering a rare blend of high efficiency and volume.\n\nWe are hunting counting stats today by leveraging the favorable matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano, who carries a 5.15 xERA. This has pushed **Luis Arraez** (66.78) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65) into the \"Strong\" tier. **Luis Arraez** is a lock at 2B, capitalizing on the +14% park factor and the premium #1 spot in the order. The optimization for this slate was razor-thin at the fringes, with **Gavin Sheets** being the most difficult omission. **Gavin Sheets** (45.19) sat just outside the startable threshold because his encounter with Yoshinobu Yamamoto carries significant SP risk (-13% adjustment), which outweighed the potential for power in his projected #4 slot. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" designations, as these scores are hyper-sensitive to batting order volatility. **Cal Raleigh** (65.24) and **Daulton Varsho** (49.31) are currently reliant on mid-order protection; should either **Cal Raleigh** or **Daulton Varsho** drop in the lineup, their efficiency scores will adjust downward accordingly. Furthermore, while we are prioritizing speed, we have accepted the marginal score for **Masyn Winn** (47.54) against Shota Imanaga, as his SB profile provides a necessary floor in a category where LawDog needs to maintain its league-wide scarcity advantage. Monitor the weather in these respective venues, as any late-breaking precipitation could jeopardize the efficiency of our stack against the weaker arms in today\u2019s rotation.",
